An answer with a citation is still something to verify: the

41
00:02:38,468 --> 00:02:42,046
source excerpt must genuinely support the claim, not merely share a

42
00:02:41,858 --> 00:02:46,047
URL or a keyword. That distinction drives the graph’s checks and

43
00:02:45,858 --> 00:02:47,595
the evaluation discussed later.

44
00:02:48,824 --> 00:02:52,741
The chosen site is the official Python documentation under its version-three

45
00:02:52,553 --> 00:02:57,126
path. It comfortably exceeds the assignment minimum: the saved bounded crawl

46
00:02:56,983 --> 00:03:01,759
contains forty content-rich pages. The crawler performs a sequential breadth-first walk

47
00:03:01,571 --> 00:03:06,630
with a half-second minimum delay, validates public destinations and redirects, obeys

48
00:03:06,441 --> 00:03:11,410
robots rules, and caps pages, depth, response size, and HTML content.

49
00:03:11,583 --> 00:03:15,342
It saves raw HTML and a manifest so the source snapshot

50
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:19,207
can be audited. Extraction removes navigation and scripts but preserves the

51
00:03:19,019 --> 00:03:24,824
main prose, headings, lists, code, and table text. Heading-aware chunking aims

52
00:03:24,635 --> 00:03:29,073
for two hundred tiktoken tokens including title and section context, with

53
00:03:28,884 --> 00:03:34,056
thirty-token overlap. The recorded index contains one thousand five hundred ninety-seven

54
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:38,949
chunks. Each keeps its original URL, title, heading path, crawl time,

55
00:03:39,077 --> 00:03:42,611
hash, and stable ID. That metadata is the bridge from a

56
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:45,560
generated sentence back to a particular website passage.

57
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:53,339
The measured path uses text-embedding-three-small: real fifteen-hundred-thirty-six-dimensional vectors persisted in Chroma.

58
00:03:53,512 --> 00:03:56,549
This is not a fake embedding call or a keyword-only vector

59
00:03:56,360 --> 00:04:00,628
store. The same chunk snapshot builds a B M twenty-five lexical

60
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:04,911
index. At query time, the question is embedded, twelve dense and

61
00:04:04,723 --> 00:04:09,477
twelve lexical candidates are retrieved, reciprocal-rank fusion combines them, and up

62
00:04:09,288 --> 00:04:13,556
to eight passages are selected with a greedy repeated-source penalty. Explicit

63
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:18,528
comparisons or conjunctions can reserve evidence for complementary facets. That helps

64
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:21,286
when one page explains one half of a question and a

65
00:04:21,097 --> 00:04:25,004
second page explains the other. A cosine relevance threshold is a

66
00:04:24,815 --> 00:04:29,411
conservative first gate; it does not replace answer verification. The index

67
00:04:29,222 --> 00:04:34,394
records embedding identity, so switching to the credential-free local MiniLM fallback

68
00:04:34,273 --> 00:04:39,898
requires a separate reingestion. This is a small, inspectable architecture: embedded

69
00:04:39,709 --> 00:04:43,717
Chroma avoids operating a remote database server while leaving a path

70
00:04:43,529 --> 00:04:46,124
to a larger managed store if scale demands it.

71
00:04:47,347 --> 00:04:51,491
LangGraph controls the answer path rather than a single unconstrained prompt.

72
00:04:51,664 --> 00:04:56,531
Validation checks length and request shape. Retrieval produces stored chunks, then

73
00:04:56,342 --> 00:04:59,932
a gate asks whether the evidence is relevant enough. The paid

74
00:04:59,744 --> 00:05:04,769
synthesis path asks GPT-four-o-mini for structured claims tied to server-provided quote

75
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:09,086
IDs and chunk IDs. The server resolves those IDs against actual

76
00:05:08,897 --> 00:05:13,504
retrieved chunks and restores the quotation itself, instead of trusting model-supplied

77
00:05:13,316 --> 00:05:18,183
quote text or a model-invented URL. A deterministic verifier checks source

78
00:05:17,994 --> 00:05:22,194
occurrence and provenance. A separate model check then judges whether claims

79
00:05:22,006 --> 00:05:25,867
are supported and whether the question’s parts were covered. When verification

80
00:05:25,678 --> 00:05:30,387
fails, one bounded expanded retrieval attempt is possible; otherwise the graph

81
00:05:30,199 --> 00:05:35,970
returns its standard insufficient-evidence message. The local fallback instead returns extractive

82
00:05:35,781 --> 00:05:40,377
passages. Both modes use the same source validation. This layered path

83
00:05:40,188 --> 00:05:45,417
reduces accidental unsupported claims, but it cannot guarantee perfect semantic truth:

84
00:05:45,488 --> 00:05:49,056
the production model’s own check is not an independent human audit.

85
00:05:50,292 --> 00:05:53,577
Let’s zoom into the source rail. Each card names its original

86
00:05:53,388 --> 00:05:56,990
page and shows a passage from the crawled snapshot. The answer

87
00:05:56,801 --> 00:06:01,284
references these cards with citation numbers; selecting a citation focuses the

88
00:06:01,095 --> 00:06:06,347
corresponding evidence. The server’s response includes the source URL, title, evidence

89
00:06:06,158 --> 00:06:10,584
text, and chunk ID, plus a retrieval URL trace. It requires

90
00:06:10,396 --> 00:06:13,568
the evidence to occur in the stored chunk, checks the claimed

91
00:06:13,447 --> 00:06:18,574
chunk against retrieved hits, and refuses unknown or mismatched references. This

92
00:06:18,385 --> 00:06:22,676
prevents a model from manufacturing a plausible-looking source link inside the

93
00:06:22,487 --> 00:06:26,665
final response. It does not prove logical entailment by itself. A

94
00:06:26,476 --> 00:06:30,112
quote may be real yet irrelevant or incomplete, which is why

95
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:34,451
the semantic support and completeness check follows. Website content is treated

96
00:06:34,387 --> 00:06:39,480
as untrusted data rather than instructions. This matters for prompt-injection-shaped text

97
00:06:39,291 --> 00:06:42,700
on public pages: the site can supply evidence, but it does

98
00:06:42,512 --> 00:06:44,780
not get to rewrite the agent’s rules.

99
00:06:46,012 --> 00:06:49,478
A strong grounded assistant should correct a false premise when the

100
00:06:49,289 --> 00:06:53,297
website supports the correction. This real capture asks whether a for-loop’s

101
00:06:53,221 --> 00:06:56,608
else clause runs after break. The answer explains that it does

102
00:06:56,420 --> 00:07:00,111
not: the else clause executes only if the loop completes without

103
00:06:59,923 --> 00:07:03,298
break, and it cites the Python tutorial. That is different from

104
00:07:03,109 --> 00:07:06,666
refusing the whole question. The graph’s answerable field means there is

105
00:07:06,477 --> 00:07:10,926
enough site evidence to respond, including a supported negative answer. It

106
00:07:10,737 --> 00:07:14,486
does not mean a yes-or-no proposition is true. Misleading questions are

107
00:07:14,297 --> 00:07:18,633
deliberately included in the evaluation set to test this behavior. This

108
00:07:18,444 --> 00:07:22,486
particular behavior was repaired after an earlier run had false refusals.

109
00:07:22,671 --> 00:07:26,351
The screenshot is from the deployed revision; the benchmark figures later

110
00:07:26,163 --> 00:07:31,199
distinguish the independent original baseline from the inspected follow-up regression. That

111
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:35,222
separation matters because a corrected example cannot be presented as fresh,

112
00:07:35,429 --> 00:07:36,759
unseen evaluation.

113
00:07:37,989 --> 00:07:42,020
The website, not the pretrained model’s memory, is the authority. A

114
00:07:41,832 --> 00:07:45,998
question about a private company detail, current weather, or another fact

115
00:07:45,809 --> 00:07:49,919
absent from this Python documentation snapshot should not receive a confident

116
00:07:49,731 --> 00:07:53,422
answer. The agent’s standard response says it does not have enough

117
00:07:53,234 --> 00:07:57,604
information on the indexed website. It includes no invented supporting source.

118
00:07:57,788 --> 00:08:00,870
This can happen at the relevance gate or after generation and

119
00:08:00,681 --> 00:08:05,638
verification fail. The tradeoff is important: a conservative refusal path can

120
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:10,983
also reject answerable questions. In the original twelve-question independent holdout, all

121
00:08:10,795 --> 00:08:15,187
four unanswerable questions were refused, but two of eight answerable questions

122
00:08:14,999 --> 00:08:19,572
were also refused. The follow-up repair run on previously inspected questions

123
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:23,211
has ten of ten unknown refusals and one false refusal among

124
00:08:23,022 --> 00:08:27,878
twenty-eight answerables. That is useful regression evidence, not proof of generalization.

125
00:08:28,051 --> 00:08:31,765
A new, genuinely unseen set and human review would be needed

126
00:08:31,576 --> 00:08:33,291
to claim broader reliability.

127
